    <DataNode elementId="AT3G51820-MONOMER" textLabel="chlorophyll synthetase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38833" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;G4&lt;/i&gt; was isolated from etiolated seedlings |CITS:[8552034]|, and shown to encode for an enzyme with chlorophyll synthetase activity when heterologously expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; |CITS:[OSTER97]|. The enzyme catalyzes the esterification of both chlorophyllides a and b with identical efficiency. However their esterification was shown to occur faster in the presence of geranylgeranyl pyrophosphate (GGPP) than phytyl pyrophosphate (PhyPP). The following values were assessed for the initial esterification: 8.5 pmol.min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt;.mg&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; protein for ChlaGG and ChlbGG, and only 3.0 and 4.0 pmol.min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt;.mg&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; protein for ChlaPhy and ChlbPhy, respectively |CITS:[OSTER97]|. The esterification continued with both GGPP and PhyPP until about 90% of the substrates were esterified (20-40 min for GGPP and 40-60 min for PhyPP). The reactions stopped after about 60 min, at which time no significant difference in the yield of products esterified with PP and Phy was detectable.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G51820-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G51820.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q38833" />
